# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#
# AdGuard Home doesn't use any ${VAR} substitution in its docker-compose.yml
# at all -- there's genuinely nothing to fill in here. Everything you'd
# normally configure through environment variables (upstream DNS servers,
# blocklists, DHCP, the admin password, client rules, etc.) lives instead in
# AdGuard Home's own web UI and the config file it writes to ./confdir, which
# is why this file is basically empty. If you ever see this stack's
# docker-compose.yml grow a real ${VAR} reference, add it here -- until then
# there's nothing for render-env.sh to fill in for this stack.
